<title>NETHERLANDS: ING Q1 results in detail.</title>
<headline>ING Q1 results in detail.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>First quarter 1997</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of guilders, unless stated)</p>
<p>INSURANCE REVENUES</p>
<p>    - Life premiums (billion)		 5.20   vs    4.13</p>
<p>    - Non-life premiums (billion)	   2.32   vs    2.07</p>
<p>    - Investment/other income (bln)	 3.12   vs    2.70</p>
<p>INSURANCE PRE-TAX PROFITS</p>
<p>    - Life insurance				346  vs  308</p>
<p>    - Non-life insurance			   97  vs   59</p>
<p>    - General insurance			   208  vs  201</p>
<p>BANKING RESULTS  </p>
<p>    - Net interest revenues (billion)     1.94   vs    1.65</p>
<p>    - Revenues from securities/holdings     15   vs   34</p>
<p>    - Commission income:		    814	vs  595</p>
<p>	-- funds transfer		     162	vs  154</p>
<p>	-- securities			   258	vs  187</p>
<p>	-- insurance broking		   43	vs   35</p>
<p>	-- other				  351	vs  219</p>
<p>    - Financial transaction revenues:   328	vs  234</p>
<p>	-- securities trading		 281	vs  202</p>
<p>	-- forex dealing			 51	vs   35</p>
<p>	-- other			    loss  4	vs    3  loss</p>
<p>    - Other income			    126	vs  118</p>
<p>    - Operating expenses (billion)	  2.36   vs    1.86</p>
<p>    - Value adjustment to receivables   200	vs  275</p>
<p>    - Addition to fund for gen. risks    45	vs  nil</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
